#: game/boot.gd
msgid "Loading the world…"
msgstr ""

#: realms/ardvaun.md
msgid "The high land at the heart of the world, where the settlers made their first camps and named the ground in Land-speech. Every realm's name ends in -vaun, the Land-speech word for land."
msgstr ""

#: realms/ardvaun.md
msgid "high land, heart land"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/brekhal_varn.jsonc
msgid "The mountain pass southwest of Edhra Tewk. Its name is rocky to say, br and k, as the pass is to walk; Varn is the Land-speech word for a pass."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/brekhal_varn.jsonc
msgid "the broken pass"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/dhorvone_stolm.jsonc
msgid "A ruined castle west of Morwe Wudhen, named in Land-speech with a harsh dh, r and v. Stolm is a stronghold. Once corruption takes it, the beast-tongue seeps into its name: Dhyrvone Stolmm."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/dhorvone_stolm.jsonc
msgid "the fallen stronghold"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/edhra_tewk.jsonc
msgid "A faction outpost southeast of Lumwen Hoal, named in plain middle sounds of Land-speech for a plain place. Tewk is a camp."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/edhra_tewk.jsonc
msgid "the plain camp"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/hrovumel_stolm.jsonc
msgid "A stronghold sunk into the rock, shut for so long that nobody living remembers its halls, until a guide opens the way. Its name is hushed: a breathy hr, then round o, u and soft m and l, like air moving through a closed hall; Stolm is a stronghold."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/hrovumel_stolm.jsonc
msgid "the hushed stronghold"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/hrunde_orl.jsonc
msgid "A ring where a single beast waits to be fought. Its name is blunt and drumming, hr and nd; Orl is a ring."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/hrunde_orl.jsonc
msgid "the drumming ring"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/ivenwhal_wudhen.jsonc
msgid "A wood southeast of the foot of Brekhal Varn, its moss soaked violet with mana and ringed by gems taller than a person, where the Vynakiir den, wolves whose mana has deepened into the arcane. Its name hums in v and n like the mana in its ground, with the breathy wh of the settlers' tongue; Wudhen is their word for a wood."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/ivenwhal_wudhen.jsonc
msgid "the humming wood"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/lumwen_hoal.jsonc
msgid "The clearing where the settlers first made camp, named in Land-speech, the tongue they named the ground in. Its soft sounds, l, m and w, fit a gentle home; Hoal is the Land-speech word every clearing ends in."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/lumwen_hoal.jsonc
msgid "the soft clearing"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/lumwen_hoal.jsonc
msgid "Lumwen Hoal, corrupted. The beast-tongue has crept into the land and into its name: a y where its first vowel was, and its last sound doubled, as only beast-calls have them. Purifying it gives the clearing back its own name."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/lumwen_hoal.jsonc
msgid "the soft clearing, gone wild"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/morwe_wudhen.jsonc
msgid "A deep wood north of Lumwen Hoal. The settlers gave it dark, back vowels and the breathy dh of their tongue; Wudhen is their word for a wood."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/morwe_wudhen.jsonc
msgid "the dark wood"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/senwel_sael.jsonc
msgid "A small, quiet ground by a still pool, where only the world's testers walk. Soft sounds for a calm place; Sael is still water."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/senwel_sael.jsonc
msgid "the quiet pool"
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/thudren_orl.jsonc
msgid "A wide ring teeming with wild monsters, where the world's testers measure how much it can bear. Its name thuds like many feet; Orl is a ring."
msgstr ""

#: slices/blueprints/data/thudren_orl.jsonc
msgid "the thronging ring"
msgstr ""

