#: slices/npcs/data/people/ausvren_vo_tormaesk.jsonc
msgid "A guide of Brekhal Varn, of the Tormaesk kin, who keep the old ways through the rock. Only a Tormaesk can shift the boulders sealing the passage into Hrovumel Stolm, and Ausvren waits on the pass for someone to walk there with. The name is Hearth-speech, the everyday tongue: the given name Ausvren, soft as breath, then vo Tormaesk, of their kin, a name as hard as the stone they keep."
