#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_kalvik_kolvak.jsonc
msgid "The sharp crack of ice, then the low hiss of magma on it. Dominators called it to send their beast's two tails across a foe, one after the other."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_kalvik_kolvak.jsonc
msgid "crack, then hiss"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_kalvik_kolvak.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:kalvrakkor} whips both its tails across its target: the ice tail cracks, then the magma tail sears."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_kalvik_kolvak.jsonc
msgid "Kalvik-kolvak"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_krivvu_vrivvu.jsonc
msgid "The rumble a hound keeps up as it paces around its own, hot on one side and cold on the other. Dominators said it of a guard no foe wants to brush past."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_krivvu_vrivvu.jsonc
msgid "warm side, cold side, stay back"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_krivvu_vrivvu.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:kalvrakkor} is out, the player takes a little less harm: frost on one flank and heat on the other keep foes back."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_krivvu_vrivvu.jsonc
msgid "Krivvu-vrivvu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_lakvu_rakvu.jsonc
msgid "The bubbling of magma welling up through cracked basalt. Dominators said it of a beast that burns brighter the deeper it is cut."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_lakvu_rakvu.jsonc
msgid "it burns as it bleeds"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_lakvu_rakvu.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:kalvrakkor}'s magma runs hotter the more it's hurt, and it strikes faster."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/kalvrakkor_lakvu_rakvu.jsonc
msgid "Lakvu-rakvu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bolmu_wolmu.jsonc
msgid "The gurgle of a wet hide rolling off a blow. Dominators said it of anything that shrugs off harm and stays damp and whole."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bolmu_wolmu.jsonc
msgid "slick, it slides off"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bolmu_wolmu.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:ombulumo}'s wet skin shrugs off part of every hit."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bolmu_wolmu.jsonc
msgid "Bolmu-wolmu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bulum_bolom.jsonc
msgid "The call the first dominators shouted to send their beast leaping onto a foe. It mimics the landing: a deep thud, then the wet slap of moss settling."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bulum_bolom.jsonc
msgid "thud, then splash"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bulum_bolom.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:ombulumo} leaps and lands on its target with all its soggy weight."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_bulum_bolom.jsonc
msgid "Bulum-bolom"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_lombu_bombu.jsonc
msgid "The slow, soft breath of a resting beast, its moss swelling with every draw. Dominators said it over a wounded beast they left to sleep it off."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_lombu_bombu.jsonc
msgid "rest, and grow back"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_lombu_bombu.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:ombulumo}'s moss grows back over its wounds, and it slowly heals while it rests."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_lombu_bombu.jsonc
msgid "Lombu-bombu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_mulbo_lulbo.jsonc
msgid "A low hum the first dominators learned from their beasts, which hum it as their moss settles. Hummed back, it keeps a dominator's rings calm and slow to fade."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_mulbo_lulbo.jsonc
msgid "hush, soft moss"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_mulbo_lulbo.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:ombulumo} is out, the player's rings hold a little longer."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/ombulumo_mulbo_lulbo.jsonc
msgid "Mulbo-lulbo"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kazri_tazri.jsonc
msgid "The scrape of talons on stone as a cornered beast readies to spring. Dominators said it of anything that fights hardest once it bleeds."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kazri_tazri.jsonc
msgid "cornered, and quicker"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kazri_tazri.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:tikazzir} strikes faster the more it's hurt."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kazri_tazri.jsonc
msgid "Kazri-tazri"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kirzi_tirzi.jsonc
msgid "The chirp a beast gives when it rides the wind at its dominator's back, and the dominators' word for a light step that walks faster than it should."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kirzi_tirzi.jsonc
msgid "quick, quick, onward"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kirzi_tirzi.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:tikazzir} is out, the player walks a little faster."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_kirzi_tirzi.jsonc
msgid "Kirzi-tirzi"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_tizik_tazak.jsonc
msgid "The sharp two-note shriek of a diving beast: the high note as it folds its wings, the low one as it strikes. Dominators shouted it to send their beast down."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_tizik_tazak.jsonc
msgid "fold, then strike"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_tizik_tazak.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:tikazzir} folds its wings and drops on its target in a gust."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_tizik_tazak.jsonc
msgid "Tizik-tazak"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_zirki_kirki.jsonc
msgid "The flick of wings slipping aside. Dominators called it after a beast that was never where the blow landed."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_zirki_kirki.jsonc
msgid "flit, not here"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_zirki_kirki.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:tikazzir} dodges more often, being so light."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/tikazzir_zirki_kirki.jsonc
msgid "Zirki-kirki"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_kynri_vynri.jsonc
msgid "The whine a beast gives when its prey stands ringed and still. Dominators said it of a ring that closes before the beast inside can think to push."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_kynri_vynri.jsonc
msgid "still now, still"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_kynri_vynri.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:vynakiir} is out, the player's rings seal a little faster."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_kynri_vynri.jsonc
msgid "Kynri-vynri"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_nyvik_ryvik.jsonc
msgid "The ring of a struck crystal. Dominators called it after a beast whose brow took a blow and only sang."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_nyvik_ryvik.jsonc
msgid "it rings, and holds"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_nyvik_ryvik.jsonc
msgid "The crystal on the ${MONSTER:vynakiir}'s brow turns aside part of every mana or arcane strike."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_nyvik_ryvik.jsonc
msgid "Nyvik-ryvik"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_rynka_vynka.jsonc
msgid "The low growl a pack leader keeps up while it stands over its own. Dominators heard it at their side and held their ground."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_rynka_vynka.jsonc
msgid "stand, I am here"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_rynka_vynka.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:vynakiir} is out, the player takes a little less harm."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_rynka_vynka.jsonc
msgid "Rynka-vynka"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_vunnu_vinni.jsonc
msgid "The low hum a beast gives as its crown closes on its prey, then the high snap of its jaw. Dominators hummed it to send their beast to hold a foe still while they walked their ring around it."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_vunnu_vinni.jsonc
msgid "hum, hold, snap"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_vunnu_vinni.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:vynakiir} hums and closes its crown around its target, holding it still: it can't move or strike until the crown lets go with a snap of the jaw."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynakiir_vunnu_vinni.jsonc
msgid "Vunnu-vinni"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_mynu_vynu.jsonc
msgid "The whimper of a pup that keeps close at its packmate's heels. Dominators hummed it to a beast that stays at their side and takes the edge off every blow meant for them."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_mynu_vynu.jsonc
msgid "close, keep close"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_mynu_vynu.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:vynnimu} is out, it keeps close at the player's heels, and they take a little less harm."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_mynu_vynu.jsonc
msgid "Mynu-vynu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nimmi_nummu.jsonc
msgid "The yip a pup gives as it crouches, then the soft thump as it lands on what it pounced on. Dominators said it of any small beast that throws its whole weight at a foe twice its size."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nimmi_nummu.jsonc
msgid "yip, then thump"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nimmi_nummu.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:vynnimu} yips, crouches and pounces on its target, paws first."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nimmi_nummu.jsonc
msgid "Nimmi-nummu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nivvu_mivvu.jsonc
msgid "The squeak of a pup knocked over that rolls and springs back up. Dominators said it of a beast too soft and round to be knocked down for long."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nivvu_mivvu.jsonc
msgid "roll over, up again"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nivvu_mivvu.jsonc
msgid "The ${MONSTER:vynnimu}'s soft, round body rolls with every might strike and takes less of it."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_nivvu_mivvu.jsonc
msgid "Nivvu-mivvu"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_vummi_nummi.jsonc
msgid "The soft huffing of a pup sniffing at the dark. Dominators said it as they crept past sleeping beasts behind a nose that knew the way."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_vummi_nummi.jsonc
msgid "sniff, hush, on"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_vummi_nummi.jsonc
msgid "While the ${MONSTER:vynnimu} is out, the player's steps wake sleeping monsters less often."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/abilities/vynnimu_vummi_nummi.jsonc
msgid "Vummi-nummi"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/kalvrakkor.jsonc
msgid "The frost-and-fire hound: a heavy hound split along its spine, one side dark basalt cracked with glowing magma, the other pale ice cracked with frost, and behind it a magma tail and an ice tail. Where it lies down, the snow melts on one side and freezes hard on the other. Its name is a beast-call, the sound it makes: the crack of ice in its k's, doubled where it splits, and the low growl of its molten side in l, v and r."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/kalvrakkor.jsonc
msgid "the crack of ice, the growl of fire"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/kalvrakkor.jsonc
msgid "Kalvrakkor"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/ombulumo.jsonc
msgid "A round, soggy creature of still water that sits half-sunk in the shallows and booms at dusk, slow to rouse and hard to shift once it has. Its name is a beast-call, the sound it makes: round, soft b, m and l, and its o's and u's as deep as the boom."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/ombulumo.jsonc
msgid "the low boom from the shallows"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/ombulumo.jsonc
msgid "Ombulumo"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/tikazzir.jsonc
msgid "A small, quick flier with sharp eyes that darts low between the reeds and clicks as it turns, gone before it can be struck. Its name is a beast-call, the sound it makes: the clicks of its turns in t and k, and the buzz of its wings in the doubled z."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/tikazzir.jsonc
msgid "the click and buzz in the reeds"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/tikazzir.jsonc
msgid "Tikazzir"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/vynakiir.jsonc
msgid "A lean wolf of the high passes with a crystal on its brow and a crown of wisps turning above its head: a mana pup grown, whose crystal has hardened and whose mana has deepened into the arcane. It hunts by holding its prey still: it hums low while its crown closes on it, then snaps. Its name is a beast-call, the sound it makes: the hum in v, n and y, the howl that carries in its long ii, and the snap of its jaw in the k."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/vynakiir.jsonc
msgid "the hum that holds, then the howl"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/vynakiir.jsonc
msgid "Vynakiir"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/vynnimu.jsonc
msgid "A round, soft-footed pup of the Vynakiir, with a crystal only budding on its brow and a few wisps already drifting about its head, the start of the crown it will wear. It tumbles after its packmates through the mana moss and pounces on whatever moves, and in time it ascends into a Vynakiir, its mana deepening into the arcane. Its name is a beast-call, its whimper: the hum it shares with its elders in v, n and y, gone soft and small in the doubled n and the round u."
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/vynnimu.jsonc
msgid "the little hum that will howl"
msgstr ""

#: slices/species/data/vynnimu.jsonc
msgid "Vynnimu"
msgstr ""

